<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%">
<tr>
<td class="column-l">
<div class="fr1 mt1"><a href="./pdf/261101.pdf" target="news" onclick="gtag('config', 'UA-3981659-1', {'page_path': '/pdf/Race-result 2026/Tenno Sho (Autumn) (G1)'})">PDF(197kb)</a><img alt="" align="absmiddle" src="../_img/pdf05.gif" width="20" height="19" /></div>

<h5>Danon Decile Excels Over Strong Field in Tenno Sho (Autumn)</h5>


<div class="fr1 cb">
<!--
<a href="javascript:writeGallery('Nov. 1, 2026','Tenno Sho (Autumn) (G1)','../en/racing/news_media/gallery/img/2026/s2/261101a.jpg','../en/racing/news_media/gallery/img/2026/b/261101a.jpg')"><img src="./images/261101/01.jpg" width="300" height="200" alt="Tenno Sho (Autumn) (G1)" /></a><br>
<br>
-->
<a href="javascript:writeGallery('Nov. 1, 2026','Tenno Sho (Autumn) (G1)','../en/racing/news_media/gallery/img/2026/s2/261101a.jpg','../en/racing/news_media/gallery/img/2026/b/261101a.jpg')"><img src="./images/261101/02.jpg" width="300" height="200" alt="Tenno Sho (Autumn) (G1)" /></a><br>
<br>
<a href="javascript:writeGallery('Nov. 1, 2026','Tenno Sho (Autumn) (G1)','../en/racing/news_media/gallery/img/2026/s2/261101b.jpg','../en/racing/news_media/gallery/img/2026/b/261101b.jpg')"><img src="./images/261101/03.jpg" width="300" height="200" alt="Tenno Sho (Autumn) (G1)" /></a><br>
<br>
</div>



<p>Fourth favorite <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001340157/" class="link01" target="_blank">Danon Decile</a></strong> captured his third G1 title in this year&rsquo;s Tenno Sho (Autumn) becoming the first horse since Symboli Kris S in 2003 to score the win from the widest draw. In 2024, the son of Epiphaneia topped the three-year-olds when claiming the Tokyo Yushun (Japanese Derby, G1, 2,400m) and added another G1 victory in the Dubai Sheema Classic (G1, 2,410m) the next spring. After posting a fifth in the International Stakes (G1, 2,050m) in Great Britain last summer, he continued to struggle marking four consecutive third-place finishes at G1 level—the Japan Cup (2,400m) and the Arima Kinen (2,500m) last year, then the Osaka Hai (2,000m) and the Takarazuka Kinen (2,200m) this spring. Trainer Shogo Yasuda registered his third JRA-G1 title after this year&rsquo;s Sprinters Stakes with Puro Magic while jockey Keita Tosaki tallied his 16th G1 title following his success in the Shuka Sho with Monroe Walk two weeks earlier. This victory marked their first Tenno Sho titles in both the spring and autumn editions.</p>
<p>Breaking smoothly from the farthest stall, <strong>Danon Decile</strong> was unhurried in second from the rear before launching his bid with a wide sweeping move into the straight. From there, with a tremendous burst of speed, the son of Epiphaneia thundered down the stretch, taking command over his rivals rallying for the lead at the furlong pole and held off a late challenge by the runner-up to prevail by a 2-1/2-length margin.</p>
<p>&ldquo;To be honest, the widest draw took us by surprise and we were forced to change tactics, but today, the most important factor was to keep him in good rhythm, which he did, fortunately. He responded a bit earlier than I hoped but he stayed on to the wire and I&rsquo;m truly happy that he was able to show his true ability at last,&rdquo; commented Keita Tosaki after the race.</p>
<p>Half-brother to 2019 Horse of the Year Lys Gracieux, eighth pick <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001355496/" class="link01" target="_blank">Nebra Disk</a></strong> saved ground around 12th early and although meeting traffic in early stretch, responded well in the last 300 meters to briefly threaten <strong>Danon Decile</strong>. While no match for the winner&rsquo;s late speed, the son of Duramente secured the runner-up spot, 3/4 lengths over Regaleira.</p>
<p>Third favorite and sole mare <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001337645/" class="link01" target="_blank">Regaleira</a></strong> traveled in front of <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001354311/" class="link01" target="_blank">Masquerade Ball</a></strong> and <strong>Nebra Disk </strong>earlier and after entering the stretch, found an opening just on the rails to launch her late charge. The Suave Richard mare joined the rally passing the 200-meter pole but was overtaken by the winner and failed to close in on the eventual runner-up while holding off the rest of the field by 1-1/4 lengths for third place.</p>
<p>Race favorite <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001352760/" class="link01" target="_blank">Croix Du Nord</a></strong> took a ground-saving trip after breaking from the innermost stall in around sixth position from the front. As the field bunched up heading into the straight, the multiple G1 winner in tight quarters angled off the rails but continued to struggle behind horses into the last furlong and was unable to display his trademark turn of foot, finishing fifth.</p>
<p><u>Other Horses:</u><br>
 4th: (14) <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001335745/" class="link01" target="_blank">Tagano Dude</a></strong>—trailed in rear, angled out to launch 2nd fastest late drive but belatedly<br>
 6th: (11) <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001319644/" class="link01" target="_blank">Shake Your Heart</a></strong>—sat wide in front of winner, passed tired rivals<br>
 7th: (8) <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001305177/" class="link01" target="_blank">Jun Blossom</a></strong>—ran around 12th, circled wide, lacked needed kick<br>
 8th: (15) <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001352772/" class="link01" target="_blank">Sakura Farrel</a></strong>—traveled wide around 9th, accelerated until 100m out<br>
 9th: (12) <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001338613/" class="link01" target="_blank">Cosmo Kuranda</a></strong>—tracked leaders around 3rd, showed effort but even paced in last 100m<br>
 10th: (6) <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001310212/" class="link01" target="_blank">Seiun Hades</a></strong>—settled around 6th, joined rally for lead briefly, weakened thereafter<br>
 11th: (7) <strong>Masquerade Ball</strong>—unhurried around 14th, struggled to find clear path in stretch<br>
 12th: (16) <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001357974/" class="link01" target="_blank">Giovanni</a></strong>—sat near pace from widest draw, checked by rival 200m out, lost momentum<br>
 13th: (5) <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001326093/" class="link01" target="_blank">Champagne Color</a></strong>—raced near rear, switched to outside at early stretch, never fired<br>
 14th: (9) <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001325914/" class="link01" target="_blank">Ho O Biscuits</a></strong>—chased leaders in 3rd, sustained bid up to 200m pole<br>
 15th: (13) <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001372443/" class="link01" target="_blank">Realize Sirius</a></strong>—stalked pace in 2nd, dropped back in last 400m<br>
 16th: (2) <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001320356/" class="link01" target="_blank">Elton Barows</a></strong>—traveled around 7th, checked by rival at early stretch, showed little<br>
 17th: (4) <strong><a href="https://www.jbis.jp/horse/0001360434/" class="link01" target="_blank">Readiness</a></strong>—set pace, used up after climbing up hill</p>
<div class="fr1 c">
 <img src="./images/261101/racecourse.jpg" width="132" height="69" alt="">
</div>

<p><strong>THE 174TH TENNO SHO (AUTUMN) (G1)</strong><br>
 3-year-olds &amp; up, 2,000 meters (about 10 furlongs), turf, left-handed<strong></strong><br>
 Sunday, November 1, 2026      Tokyo Racecourse        11th Race         Post time: 15:40<br>
 Total prize money: &yen; 651,000,000 (about US$ 4,200,000 &lt;US$1=&yen;155&gt;)<br>
 3-y-o: 56kg (about 123-124 lbs), 4-y-o &amp; up: 58kg (about 128 lbs),<br>
 2kg allowance for Fillies &amp; Mares, 2kg allowance for Southern Hemisphere-bred born in 2023<br>
 Course record: 1:55.2              Race record: 1:55.2 [Equinox (JPN, by Kitasan Black), 2023]<br>
 Safety factor: 18 runners          Going: Good to Firm      Weather: Fine</p>
